# Changelog

All notable changes to Ocelotl are documented in this file.

The project follows [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/). Changes that have been merged since the latest tag remain under **Unreleased** until a version is approved, tagged, and published.

## [Unreleased]

### Added

- Automated R environment provisioning, including R, optional RStudio Desktop, system dependencies, and configured CRAN, Bioconductor, and GitHub packages.
- Visual Studio Code installation with Nextflow, Nextflow Sandbox, YAML, and Ansible extensions.
- Zsh and Oh My Zsh configuration with autosuggestions, syntax highlighting, and common terminal tools.
- Ansible development tooling through the new `ansible` role, including `ansible-lint`.
- Ubuntu 26.04 support in the bootstrap operating-system check, alongside Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04.
- Obsidian installation from official release artifacts.
- Godot installation with a command symlink and desktop integration.
- Syncthing installation from its official APT repository, with its user service enabled.
- MIT License.

### Fixed

- The bootstrap now launches the main workstation playbook after completing prerequisite checks and ensuring Ansible is available.
- Docker provisioning reloads systemd units after repository and socket migration, preventing stale unit state on an existing workstation.

## [1.0.0] - 2026-08-06

### Added

- Modular Ansible role architecture.
- Bootstrap prerequisite checks and automatic Ansible Core installation.
- Common system package provisioning.
- Conda installation, configuration, and verification.
- Java installation and verification.
- Docker installation, configuration, and verification.
- Nextflow installation and verification.
- Idempotent provisioning and modular verification tasks.
- Use of official software repositories and release artifacts.

[Unreleased]: https://github.com/erickdelgadillo/ocelotl/compare/v1.0.0...HEAD
[1.0.0]: https://github.com/erickdelgadillo/ocelotl/tree/v1.0.0
